          "entities": {},
          "text": "DeepSeek Harness, AKA DSH, treats memory as a first-class plugin, not a hidden subsystem.\n\nThis means memory can be installed, swapped, benchmarked, and composed like any other capability.\n\nAgents shouldn’t start from zero every session. They should accumulate experience.\n\nEverOS is now #8 on the dsh-plugin list. We’re just getting started.\n\nFor some reasons, I think as a name DSH is way cooler than DeepSeek Harness. 😎"
        },
